  "mathematical_result": "Sections 15.6.4 and 29.12.3 develop convergence for every smooth obstacle. The resulting uniformity is covariant under smooth gauges and positive scaling, and its analytic closure is exactly ordinary/ideal envelope equality for all smooth obstacles. On curves this closure equals the zero-obstacle closure. The new pseudometric has complete canonical ideal loci, while the whole ordinary space remains incomplete even on a fixed positive-mass model family. On ordinary curve models its topology is strictly between the zero-obstacle topology and polar total variation.",
  "limitations": "All-obstacle convergence restores smooth-gauge covariance but remains nonseparated on ordinary classes and incomplete on general curve models. Its analytic closure requires equality at every smooth obstacle; this is equivalent to zero-obstacle equality on curves, while the higher-dimensional implication is not proved. Polar total variation remains the stronger complete curve-model topology.",
